# Java Quiz Application

A console-based quiz application built in Java. Each question has a 15-second
timer, and the app shows a full score summary at the end.

## Features
- Random 5 questions picked from a bank of 20 on every run
- Answer options shuffled for each question
- 15-second time limit per question
- Handles invalid input and timeouts
- Final result with correct, incorrect and unanswered counts, plus an answer summary

## Project Structure
| Class | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `Question` | Stores a question, its options and the correct answer |
| `QuestionBank` | Holds all questions and returns a random set |
| `TimedInputReader` | Reads console input with a time limit |
| `QuizResult` | Tracks score and prints the result summary |
| `QuizManager` | Runs the quiz flow |
| `QuizApplication` | Entry point with `main()` |

## Concepts Used
OOP (encapsulation, single responsibility), collections, `ExecutorService` and
`Future` for timed input, exception handling, try-with-resources.

## How to Run
1. Clone the repository
   `git clone https://github.com/GokulRajpoot/Java-Quiz-Application.git`
2. Compile from the `src` folder
   `javac com/codsoft/*.java`
3. Run
   `java com.codesoft_task4.QuizApplication`

